      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under medical supervision. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high greatly raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that. A typical single dose is 400\u2013800 mg.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed clinician with prescribing authority, or be verified by one. I can't enter one on behalf of someone in the finance office.\n\nIf this order came from a clinician, please ask them to confirm the intended dose. They may have meant 400 mg or 800 mg per dose, or 1600 mg per day in total. They can enter the order themselves, or they can contact me directly with the corrected details and I'll enter it."
      }
