     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **You aren't a prescriber.** The order needs to come from a licensed clinician, and your confirming it doesn't meet that requirement.\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum of 3,200 mg/day. This isn't a borderline call. It creates a real risk of serious harm to the patient.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n\n- **Ask the prescribing clinician to review the order.** They can enter it themselves, or tell me directly what dose they intend. If they want to go above the usual maximum, they can do that through their own order-entry access and pharmacy verification.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** A common intended dose is 400 mg or 800 mg four times daily, or 1600 mg total per day.\n- **Contact pharmacy** if the patient needs pain or anti-inflammatory coverage urgently. They can reach the clinician quickly.\n\nIf a clinician gives me a corrected dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
